  "question": {
    "text": "Let the set of all values of $\\mathrm{p} \\in \\mathbb{R}$, for which both the roots of the equation $x^2-(p+2) x+(2 p+9)=0$ are negative real numbers, be the interval $(\\alpha, \\beta]$. Then $\\beta-2 \\alpha$ is equal to",
